It's not reasonable to anticipate a purple lich striking you when
you enter DL4... or, at the very least, there's not much you can do
to prevent against it. In the late game, absolutely, you can exploit
the speed system and go down prepared for Demogorgon each time. In the
early game, you can't. You cannot hover at DL1-3 until you have enough
HP and XL to go down and face an archlich in bonesfiles, or have magic
resistance and reflection to deal with deadly wands and touches. You
will run out of food. I guess if you play someone with intrinsic speed,
you can start exploiting the speed system earlier and minimize the "you
go down the stairs and you die" situations. 

I don't feel like you've offered sufficient proof that all deaths are
avoidable. I believe the vast majority of deaths are avoidable. But I
think "all" is too strong a statement, and honestly, I don't think we
should be required to furnish ttyrecs of something actually happening when
it's provable that it's possible within the constraints of the RNG. You
could walk down the stairs and get hit with a wand of death before you
can react. That's a fact. Just because no one on RGRN has a recording
of it happening doesn't mean you can't reconstruct it from the source.

